# Connection limit per client address on port 9000 for a network. The limit
# is per IPv4 address or per IPv6 /64 inside the network. The longest prefix
# wins. 0 means no limit. Networks that are not in this file get 64.
#
# <network> <connections>
# 203.0.113.0/24 256
# 2001:db8:1::/48 0
